          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: hervir",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "hervir — \"to boil\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Herví el agua para la pasta. I boiled the water for the pasta."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Stem change: hiervo, hirvió. El agua está hirviendo — the water is boiling."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "hervir is inherited from Latin fervēre 'to boil, to seethe' (EtymDB), through old Spanish herver. Latin f- became Spanish h-. English fervent comes from the same verb."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
